    "generalInformation": "CDU is a private, non-profit university located in Willowbrook, California, an unincorporated area of south Los Angeles County between the City of Compton and the Watts neighborhood. The institution was founded in 1966 after a report by the McCone Commission cited poor health status and diminished access to quality education, healthcare, employment, and public safety services as key factors sparking the 1965 revolt in Watts and adjacent communities (\u201cViolence in the City: An End or a Beginning\u201d \u2013 Governor Edmund G. Brown). ",
    "missionStatement": "\u2022\tThe mission of the College of Medicine is to provide education, research and clinical service in the context of community engagement in order to train physician leaders who promote wellness, who provide care with excellence and compassion, and who are committed to transforming the health of diverse and underserved communities. \n\u2022\tVision Statement: \nExcellent health and wellness for all in a world without health disparities. ",
